@startuml INA700_runtime
' INA700 - threads and their wiring
' Author: Suraj Karki
' Course: INA700 - AI-based pick and place
'
' Each thread owns one distinct job. They share nothing but bounded queues
' and one lock-guarded state object handing out immutable snapshots.

title INA700 - runtime and threading

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam class {
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BackgroundColor<<thread>> #EAF2FB
  BackgroundColor<<queue>> #FDF6E8
}

abstract class Worker <<thread>> {
  -shutdown : Event
  +{abstract} step()
  +on_start()
  +on_stop()
  +run()
}

class CaptureWorker <<thread>> {
  +step()
}
class InferenceWorker <<thread>> {
  +step()
}
class MappingWorker <<thread>> {
  +step()
}
class CycleWorker <<thread>> {
  +step()
}
class ConnectionWorker <<thread>> {
  -quit_message : str
  +step()
}

class ThreadSupervisor {
  -workers : List<Thread>
  +add(worker)
  +start_all()
  +stop_all(timeout_s)
}

class LatestResultHolder {
  +__call__() : MappedScene [0..1]
}

class "Queue<Frame>\nmaxsize=2" as FrameQueue <<queue>>
class "Queue<InferenceResult>\nmaxsize=2" as ResultQueue <<queue>>
class "Queue<MappedScene>\nmaxsize=2" as SceneQueue <<queue>>
class "Queue<PickRequest>\nmaxsize=8" as RequestQueue <<queue>>

class Container {
  +build_frame_source() : FrameSource
  +build_detector() : ObjectDetector
  +build_vision_pipeline() : VisionPipeline
  +build_coordinate_service() : CoordinateService
  +build_selector() : ObjectSelector
  +build_transport() : RobotTransport
  +build_calibrator() : SceneCalibrator [0..1]
}

Worker <|-- CaptureWorker
Worker <|-- InferenceWorker
Worker <|-- MappingWorker
Worker <|-- CycleWorker
Worker <|-- ConnectionWorker
ThreadSupervisor o-- "5" Worker

CaptureWorker --> FrameQueue : writes
InferenceWorker --> FrameQueue : reads
InferenceWorker --> ResultQueue : writes
MappingWorker --> ResultQueue : reads
MappingWorker --> SceneQueue : writes
MappingWorker --> CoordinateService
LatestResultHolder --> SceneQueue : drains
CycleController --> LatestResultHolder : get_scene
CycleWorker --> RequestQueue : reads
CycleWorker --> CycleController
InferenceWorker --> VisionPipeline
CaptureWorker --> FrameSource
ConnectionWorker --> RobotTransport

TkView --> RequestQueue : writes
TkView --> SharedState : reads snapshots
CaptureWorker --> SharedState : writes the newest image
InferenceWorker --> SharedState : writes boxes and timing
MappingWorker --> SharedState : writes live poses
CycleWorker --> SharedState : writes
ConnectionWorker --> SharedState : writes

Container ..> ThreadSupervisor : main.py wires

note bottom of ThreadSupervisor
  Tkinter must own the main thread, so the view
  is not a Worker. It polls SharedState on a
  timer and hands requests over by queue. The
  same is true of ConsoleView, which takes the
  main thread over SSH where Tk has no display.
end note

note right of FrameQueue
  Bounded at 2, and written with put_newest:
  a slow stage DROPS the stale frame rather
  than queueing it. A queue that fills would
  hand the robot a position from seconds ago.
end note

note right of CaptureWorker
  Publishes the image straight to SharedState
  as well as to the queue, so the preview stays
  live at the capture rate while the boxes drawn
  on it arrive at the inference rate.
end note

@enduml
